title: Authorizations › Ledger case page › Open and read
route: /authorizations/case/ID (a case the ledger has that is not a request)
intro: 26 of the 32 approved authorizations have no request of their own (no queue record, no Dashboard request). Their ID opens a calm summary built from the ledger record, so a row, its quick view and its review never end at 'Request not found'. It says who, which payer and service, how much of the approval is used, what is due and the next step. A case at a site the viewer is not looking at shows an out-of-site card instead.
dir: TD
also: Patient shows initials and age only, with a 'Privacy mode on' pill, as everywhere in the demo. Authorization dates are worked out from the units used and the demo clock, or taken from the ledger's own end date when it has one.
---
start s1 "Click an approved row's ID or 'Open'\nor 'Open case' in its tracked quick view or in a review drawer"
process p1 "Go to /authorizations/case/ and the case code"
decision d1 "Is the ID a request (a queue record or a Dashboard request)?"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Case page › Ways in"
decision d2 "Is the ID in the ledger?"
screen n1 "'Request not found'\n'No request R-9999' and 'Back to Authorizations'\n(only for an address typed by hand)"
endx e2 "Nothing to show for that ID"

group gPage "Ledger case page"
  screen h1 "Header\nCrumb 'Authorizations › R-0856'\nLevel chip, case ID, review type ('Continued stay 2'), status pill ('Review due'), the only status on the page\n'J.S., 51 · Summit Medicaid HMO · Residential 3.5'"
  screen m1 "Card 'Case summary', pill 'Privacy mode on'\nPatient, Payer, Service\nAuthorization: 'Thu 10/8 to Thu 10/22'\nUnits used: a bar and '12 of 14 days used, 2 left', and 'Runs out before review' in red only when the data shows it"
  screen m2 "More rows in the card\nReviews due: 'Review 2, Tue 10/20, 9:00 am' with its status pill\nNext on the clock\nApproval chance, its band, range and similar decisions"
  screen r1 "Right side\n'Next step': one sentence, for example 'Review 2 is drafted. Read it, then sign it. Cadence books the next one.'\n'History' (folded, closed at first): '4 entries. Latest: ...'\nOpened: approval, drafts, signatures, and what comes next (dashed)"
  click ch "Click the 'History' header, or press Enter or Space on it"
  process pch "Timeline shows; click again to fold it"
  process u1 "Case not approved yet: Authorization and Units used say 'Not approved yet'\nReviews due says 'None until the request is approved'\n(no case reaches it at the start: each one not approved is also a request)"
  process u2 "After a signature: a 'Next review' line shows the date Cadence booked"
endgroup

decision d3 "Is a review due this week and not yet signed?"
click c1 "Click 'Open the review'"
process p2 "Go to /authorizations?view=reviews&review= and the review ID\nThe drawer opens over Reviews this week"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Reviews this week › The review drawer"
process p3 "No 'Open the review' button\n(the review is signed, or none is due)"
click c2 "Click 'Back to Authorizations' or the crumb 'Authorizations'"
process p4 "Go to /authorizations\nThe last view and filters used come back"
goto g3 "Continues in: Authorizations › Worklist › Arrive and read the views"
goto g4 "Continues in: Authorizations › Ledger case page › Workflow line and history"
end e1 "Case is read"

s1 --> p1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| g1
d1 -->|No| d2
d2 -->|No| n1 --> e2
d2 -->|Yes| h1 --> m1 --> m2 --> r1
m1 -.->|A case that follows a payer workflow| g4
r1 --> ch --> pch
m1 -.-> u1
m2 -.-> u2
r1 --> d3
d3 -->|Yes| c1 --> p2 --> g2
d3 -->|No| p3
r1 --> c2 --> p4 --> g3
p3 --> e1
c2 -.-> e1
